on paper solo a star wars story wasn't  the worst idea but in practice the  project didn't really work out the han  solo star wars prequel was released in  may 2018 to a less than enthusiastic  reception becoming one of the worst  performing movies in the entire series  far from the billion dollar heights of  the force awakens solo brought in only  about 393 million at the global box  office a shockingly low sum for what  used to be the biggest movie franchise  in the world prior to the launch of solo  it was reported that disney was working  on other spin-offs focusing on different  characters from the franchise including  obi-wan kenobi and boba fett the boba  fett movie was even reported as having a  writer director attached in james  mangold who previously held the  well-received logan in 2017  but after solo crashed and burned those  plans seemed to have changed and at this  point we'd be surprised if they ever  went back to it if audiences cared so  little about solo it's hard to imagine  them getting excited for boba fett  imagine a movie that combined cowboys  ninjas and vikings starring chris pratt  in the lead role as the cowboy ninja  viking sounds fun enough right well it  wasn't meant to be based on a 2009  limited series from image comics cowboy  ninja viking was announced by universal  pitchers in 2017 and then delayed  indefinitely in august 2018 only a month  before production had been set to start  pratt was slated to play the main  character duncan a super soldier with a  personality disorder splitting his  identity into three distinct power sets  it was originally set for release in  june 2019 with a budget of around 65  million dollars but was reportedly  plagued by script issues which helped  lead to its collapse according to the  hollywood reporter rumors of the film's  impending shutdown flew around hollywood  for months meaning it wasn't too much of  a surprise that the movie didn't come  together even if it's disappointing for  fans of the comic  supernatural goth comic adaptation the  crow hit theaters in 1994 and it feels  like hollywood has been trying to remake  the movie ever since but every time it  starts to come together the project hits  a wall a revolving door of actors has  been attached or been rumored to be  attached to the role of undead avenger  eric draven which was first made popular  by brandon lee the list includes tom  hiddleston alexander skarsgard luke  evans jack houston and more and that's  not even getting into all of the  potential directors who have come and  gone production was finally set to begin  in 2015 before the bankruptcy of  production company relativity media shut  the project down by late 2016 financing  had reportedly been secured for another  attempt with jason momoa in the lead  role and the nuns coryn hardy in the  director's chair in march 2018 variety  reported that sony was setting a release  date for the crow for october 2019 but  just over two months later deadline  broke the news that momoa and hardy had  moved on not long after that sony took  the movie off its schedule  neil blomkamp made a huge impression in  2009 with his debut feature the sci-fi  parable district 9. while he's since  produced two more full-length movies  with elysium and chappie he also makes  short films with his company oat studio  in 2017 the company made a 27-minute  short called firebase set during the  vietnam war and focusing on some  american soldiers who experienced some  very freaky occurrences they were  monsters  in the shaving man  now they wouldn't die after the short  was released online it was announced  that the studio planned to adapt it into  a full-length feature if a crowdfunding  drive was successful enough long story  short it wasn't in april 2018 oates  studio tweeted the news that the longer  version of firebase was dead and that  all contributors would have their money  refunded as they wrote in their  sense-deleted message unfortunately we  didn't raise enough to do something  truly awesome we would rather over  deliver than create an average film we  thank the thousands of people who did  back us  check out one of our newest videos right  here plus even more looper videos about  your favorite stuff are coming soon  subscribe to our youtube channel and hit  the bell so you don't miss a single one  [Music]
 

